Falsifies `machine_discovery::acpi::region::verification::no_read_leaves_the_region`.

The defect: the bound check tests where the read starts instead of where it ends. A read
whose first byte is inside the region and whose length runs past the far edge is then
accepted, and the slice index panics on the boot path. This is the shape a reader reaches
for while tidying: "the address is inside the region" is true and is not the condition the
length needs. A host test of the one boundary catches it too, but the proof covers every
base, address and length at once.

Expected to fail: `assert!(offset + len <= N as u64)`, or the slice index inside `read`.

diff --git a/crates/machine_discovery/src/acpi/region.rs b/crates/machine_discovery/src/acpi/region.rs
--- a/crates/machine_discovery/src/acpi/region.rs
+++ b/crates/machine_discovery/src/acpi/region.rs
@@ -123,7 +123,7 @@
             .checked_sub(self.first)
             .ok_or(RegionError::OutsideRegion)?;
         let offset_end = end - self.first;
-        if offset_end > self.bytes.len() as u64 {
+        if offset > self.bytes.len() as u64 {
             return Err(RegionError::OutsideRegion);
         }
         // Both offsets are at most `bytes.len()`, which is a `usize`, so the casts cannot truncate.
